<title>USA: ATA to start Orlando/Grand Rapids service.</title>
<headline>ATA to start Orlando/Grand Rapids service.</headline>
<dateline>INDIANAPOLIS 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>American Trans Air Inc (ATA), the principal unit of Amtran Inc, said Tuesday it will start a seasonal non-stop flight between Kent County International Airport in Grand Rapids, Mich. and Orlando, Florida.</p>
<p>The service will run from January 24 to April 20. It said it will operate flights three days a week.</p>
<p>ATA said it will offer introductory one-way fares of $109.</p>
<p>--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787</p>
</text>
